  "verbalization": "Nilvadipine is shown to interact with Cyp2e1 through binding, which is a common mechanism in drug-target interactions. This binding leads to the participation of Cyp2e1 in various enzymatic activities, including arachidonic acid epoxygenation and monooxygenation, as well as steroid hydroxylation. These activities are all mediated by Cyp2c19, suggesting a complex network of interactions where Nilvadipine influences the function of Cyp2c19 through its interaction with Cyp2e1. The consistent scores across the three paths indicate a strong, reliable relationship between Nilvadipine and Cyp2c19, with the shared involvement of Cyp2e1 acting as a critical intermediary. The mechanistic pathway highlights the importance of Cyp2e1 in the metabolic processes that ultimately affect Cyp2c19, providing a clear and direct link between Nilvadipine and its target enzyme.",
